+\section{Fusion and KPI Results}
+\label{sec:fusionresults}
+The power of sensor fusion is that hard negatives rarely fool every modality in the same way. Radar can overreact to birds or RC fixed-wing aircraft, acoustic cues can be unreliable in weather/traffic noise, passive RF can be missing or contaminated by RFI, and GBAD-style cueing can be stale or horizon-limited. A late-fusion comparator aggregates those branch strengths while preserving train/CV-only threshold selection. EI then searches the same detector-view score space for sparse calibrated combinations that better match the low-FPR objective.
